  <!-- SECTION 4: WHAT SUCCESS MEANS -->
  <div class="section" id="success">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">04 — What Success Looks Like to Customers</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Customers define success as behavioral change, not platform activation.</h2>
      <p class="section-tagline">When asked what they need to see to consider Adaptive a success, customers overwhelmingly point to outcomes downstream of the platform: reduced phishing click rates, employees who recognize attacks and report them, and training that runs without constant admin effort. The onboarding experience needs to build a direct bridge from setup to those outcomes.</p>
    </div>

