  <!-- SECTION 5: WHAT THEY NEED -->
  <div class="section" id="help">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-num">05 — What Customers Need From Adaptive to Succeed</span>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Support, check-ins, and content freshness. Not more features — more partnership.</h2>
      <p class="section-tagline">When asked "what can Adaptive do to help you be successful," customers did not primarily ask for new capabilities. They asked for ongoing responsiveness, proactive check-ins, best practice guidance, and evidence that the content will keep up with the threat landscape. The relationship they want is partner, not vendor.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="accent-block c1-border">
          <div class="block-title">Regular check-ins and proactive outreach</div>
          <div class="block-body">Quarterly business reviews, bi-monthly calls, and post-launch check-ins appeared in dozens of responses. Customers are not asking for hand-holding — they are asking for a structured cadence that surfaces problems before they fester and keeps them current on new capabilities they may not know exist.</div>
